 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a license\nto sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises",
    "basePrintNo": "S8897",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8897-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §64, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8897\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to a\nlicense to sell liquor at retail for consumption on certain premises\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe bill creates an exception to the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law,\nallowing a license to be issued to a location that had previously been\nissued a license at its current premises.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSubdivision 7 of section 64 of the Alcoholic Beverage Control Law is\namended by adding a new paragraph (e-14).\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWhile the Alcoholic Beverage Control law prohibits the sale for on-prem-\nises consumption of alcohol at any location within 200 feet of a build-\ning occupied exclusively as a school, this bill will allow the State\nLiquor Authority to issue a license to a location that had previously\nbeen issued a license. Other exceptions have been made for certain\nestablishments and do not pose problems for the buildings being occupied\nexclusively as a school.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
